course: dictionary
lesson: 10275
title: Context clues: the word tor
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A tor is a small hill with a pile of bare, weathered rock on top, mostly found in south-west England on Dartmoor and Bodmin Moor. You can work out the meaning from context: «Haytor» and «Hound Tor» are place names, and the Ten Tors challenge is a hike, so tor must be a place you walk up, not an animal or a person.
explain: The same spelling can mean something different in another language. In Ruvan, «Pela-n mika tor» means the dog sees the girl. Here tor means sees. Check the other words first: mika is girl and pela is dog, so the ending -n shows who is doing the action.
explain: Word order can change who does the action, but the meaning of tor stays the same. «Mika-n pela tor» means the girl sees the dog, because -n now marks mika as the doer. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A tor is a small hill topped with a pile of bare, weathered rock.
fact: Tors are mostly found in south-west England, on Dartmoor and Bodmin Moor.
fact: Tors are made of granite that frost, rain and wind have worn into rounded blocks over millions of years.
fact: The Ten Tors is a famous hiking challenge for teenagers.
fact: In Ruvan, «tor» means sees, so the same spelling can have a different meaning in another language.
exercise: «We stood on top of the tor and looked across Dartmoor.» What is a tor? | A deep river valley | *A small hill topped with bare, weathered rock | A large kind of tree | A stone path in a town
exercise: In Ruvan, «Mika-n pela tor» means the girl sees the dog. What does tor mean in this sentence? | Girl | Dog | A hill | *Sees
exercise: Which of these is a place name that includes the word Tor? | *Haytor | Snowdon Station | Tower Bridge | Big Ben
test: Where are most tors found in England? | Norfolk beaches | *South-west England, on Dartmoor and Bodmin Moor | Northern Scotland | London parks
test: In «Pela-n mika tor», what does tor mean? | Girl | *Sees | Hill | Dog
exam: What are the Ten Tors? | *A famous hiking challenge for teenagers | Ten bags of rock | A type of granite cake | A river in Wales
